<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n37184" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">possessor</span></b> , ōris, m.
		id., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a
				possessor</i> (class.) </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>, <i><span class="en">Cic. Phil.
				5, 7, 20</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">bonorum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. Quint. 8, 30</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">regni inertis,</span>”
				i. e. <i>Pluto</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Luc.
					6, 779</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Hor. Ep. 1, 2,
			49</span></i>.—Esp. t. t. in law (post-Aug.), <i>the possessor of the thing claimed;</i> hence, <i>the defendant</i> in a suit (opp. petitor), <i><span class="en">Plin. Ep. 6,
				2, 2</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Quint. 7, 1, 38</span></i>;
					<i><span class="en">Paul. Sent. 5, 36,
			1</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Aquilo possessor Italici litoris,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Petr. 114</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
